[about]
Title=1 - User Interface
Intro=EdSharp's one window, the edit box you hear, dialogs that all work one way, and where help is, each named and then shown by the reader; then the rules every key follows, so a key can be guessed before it is learned.
Setup=EdSharp is open, with an empty document.
Homework=Open EdSharp and name each thing as you reach it: the title, the edit box, the status line.

[step]

Say=One want: to move around EdSharp without hunting. Everything in it follows a few rules, and this walk shows each one as the screen reader hears it.
Key=
[step]

Say=EdSharp is one window. The document you are editing fills it, and its name is in the title. The edit box is a plain Windows edit control, so every reader reads it the same way.
Key=Insert+Tab
Hear=EdSharp, Untitled, edit, multiline, blank
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.
[step]

Say=Other documents you open wait behind this one. Control plus Tab moves to the next, and the reader says its name.
Key=Control+Tab
Hear=Notes dot txt, edit, multiline
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.
[step]

Say=F4 lists every open document by name, so you can choose one rather than cycle through them.
Key=F4
Hear=Pick Window dialog, list box, Notes dot txt, 1 of 2
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.
[step]

Say=Escape returns to the document, with nothing changed.
Key=Escape
Hear=Notes dot txt, edit, multiline
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.
[step]

Say=Two keys say where you are. Alt plus A, Say Address, gives the line, the column, and how far down the document you are.
Key=Alt+A
Hear=Line 1, column 1, 0 percent
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.
[step]

Say=Alt plus Z, Say Status, says whether the document has changed since it was saved.
Key=Alt+Z
Hear=Not modified
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.
[step]

Say=Pressed twice, Alt plus Z says the file's character encoding, the way its letters are stored.
Key=Alt+Z
Hear=UTF-8
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.
[step]

Say=EdSharp speaks its own confirmations as they happen, such as Converting, or a bookmark's place. They are shown on the status line too, so a message missed can be read again with the reader's own key for that line.
Key=Insert+Page Down
Hear=Line 1 of 1
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.
[step]

Say=Every dialog works the same way. Control plus O, Open, shows the Windows Open dialog you already know.
Key=Control+O
Hear=Open dialog
Hear=File name: edit combo
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.
[step]

Say=A label and its control, Tab between them, Alt with the underlined letter to jump to one, Control plus Enter for OK from anywhere, and Escape to cancel.
Key=Escape
Hear=Notes dot txt, edit, multiline
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.
[step]

Say=Text boxes that ask for something remember your answers. Control plus J, Jump to Line, asks for a line number.
Key=Control+J
Hear=Jump to Line dialog, Line: edit, 120
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.
[step]

Say=The box already holds my last answer, 120. Up and Down Arrows bring back earlier ones, newest first.
Key=Up Arrow
Hear=40
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.
[step]

Say=Escape, and I am back where I was.
Key=Escape
Hear=Notes dot txt, edit, multiline
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.
[step]

Say=Selection is spoken as you make it. Shift with Down Arrow selects a line.
Key=Shift+Down Arrow
Hear=The budget for the second quarter is attached. selected
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.
[step]

Say=Shift plus Space, Say Selected, reads what is selected. Pressed twice, it spells it.
Key=Shift+Space
Hear=The budget for the second quarter is attached.
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.
[step]

Say=Control plus Space selects the chunk at the cursor, a run of characters with no spaces in it, such as a web address; pressed again, it adds the next.
Key=
[step]

Say=Help is in four places, and they are the same in every Homer program. F1 opens the guide, the whole program in one document.
Key=F1
Hear=EdSharp Guide
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.
[step]

Say=Shift plus F1 opens the history of changes; Alt plus F1 says the version, and offers a newer one if there is one; Control plus Shift plus F1 opens the quick starts, one for each kind of work.
Key=Alt+F1
Hear=About EdSharp dialog
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.
[step]

Say=Escape closes it. The Help menu, F10 then H, holds all of these, and Play Tutorials, which plays these walks.
Key=Escape
Hear=Notes dot txt, edit, multiline
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.
[step]

Say=Every key is named for a word in its command: Control plus O for Open, Control plus F for Find, Control plus K for bookmark. A key never comes from the middle of a word.
Key=
[step]

Say=Control plus F1 is the Key Describer. While it is on, every key says what it does instead of doing it: the safe way to explore the keyboard.
Key=Control+F1
Hear=Key Describer on
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.
[step]

Say=Now Control plus O only says what it would do.
Key=Control+O
Hear=Control plus O, Open a file
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.
[step]

Say=Control plus F1 again turns the describer off.
Key=Control+F1
Hear=Key Describer off
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.
[step]

Say=Alt plus F10 is the Alternate Menu: every command in one list you type into, with its key beside it.
Key=Alt+F10
Hear=Alternate Menu
Hear=Command, list box, 1 of 222
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.
[step]

Say=I type the word convert, and the list narrows to the commands with that word.
Key=convert
Hear=Text Convert, Control plus T, 1 of 9
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.
[step]

Say=Escape closes the list without running anything. Configuration Options, Alt plus Shift plus C, holds every setting, each a labelled control, so a setting is found by its name.
Key=Escape
Hear=Notes dot txt, edit, multiline
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.
[step]

Say=A short review. I say a command; the reader says its key. Save As.
Key=
Hear=Control plus Shift plus S
[step]

Say=Jump to Line.
Key=
Hear=Control plus J
[step]

Say=Replace.
Key=
Hear=Control plus R
[step]

Say=Say the path of this file.
Key=
Hear=Alt plus P
[step]

Say=Say the time.
Key=
Hear=Alt plus Semicolon
[step]

Say=Copy the whole document.
Key=
Hear=Control plus F8
[step]

Say=Every one of these is in Hotkeys, in the Help menu, listed three ways: by key, by command, and by menu.
Key=
